From fdacfec850c21b55d16007b8340f4165f799bac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:19:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tools: add optional tenant argument for single-node instances
 behind a proxy

A single-node VictoriaMetrics has no tenants, but an authenticating proxy
in front of it (for example vmauth with `tenants: [...]` or `tenants: all`
users) lets the client pick the tenant with the AccountID and ProjectID
request headers. The metrics tools had no way to set them, so such users
always got the proxy's 400. mcp-victorialogs and mcp-victoriatraces already
have a `tenant` tool argument that is sent as these headers.

Add the same optional `tenant` string argument (format AccountID:ProjectID,
AccountID alone is accepted too) to every tool that queries a single-node
instance, and send it as AccountID/ProjectID after the headers from
MCP_PASSTHROUGH_HEADERS, so the argument wins over a forwarded header. The
value is parsed with auth.NewToken (also used for VM_DEFAULT_TENANT_ID)
and refused before any request is made when it is not numeric.

When the argument is absent nothing is sent: existing setups are unchanged.
Cluster and cloud modes keep their path-based tenant argument.
