diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 15b6f2b..5a5e273 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -644,6 +644,14 @@ This is the main source of resource usage. To reduce it, add `documentation` to
 
 You can use `MCP_PASSTHROUGH_HEADERS` parameter in the MCP Server together with [Header-based routing in vmauth](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/vmauth/#routing-by-header) to route MCP calls between instances based on HTTP header values from your MCP client config.  
 
+### How to choose a tenant when `VM_INSTANCE_TYPE` is `single`?
+
+A single-node instance has no tenants of its own, but an authenticating proxy in front of it, such as [vmauth](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/vmauth/), can map several tenants onto it
+and let the client choose with the `AccountID` and `ProjectID` request headers. For this case every tool that queries the instance has an optional `tenant` argument (format `AccountID:ProjectID`, both 32-bit integers).
+When set, the MCP server sends it as the `AccountID` and `ProjectID` headers (after the headers from `MCP_PASSTHROUGH_HEADERS`, so the argument wins);
+when omitted, no tenant headers are sent. An invalid value is refused before any request is made.
+In `cluster` mode the tenant is part of the URL path instead, as before.
+
 ## Roadmap
 
 - [x] Support "Prettify query" tool (done in [`v0.0.5`](https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/mcp-victoriametrics/releases/tag/v0.0.5))
